To run this test, execute the script ```runall```.

This simulation requires sumo-launchd to be running.

There is a static SatCar at 0,0,0 and a static LEO Satellite at a position defined by ```configureTest.py```, also see ```omnetpp.ini```.
After 3s of simulation time the LEO satellite transmits a packet and after 4s of simulation time the SatCar transmits a packet.
Depending on the elevationAngle between both (antenna height of the SatCar is considered) the SatCar and the LEO satellite, the packets are either received or not.
Packets are received when the elevationAngle between SatCar antenna and LEO satellite exceeds or is equal to (>=) a threshold called minElevationAngle.
In this test, the minElevationAngle is 25deg.
The test also compares if the computed elevation angle between SatCar antenna and LEO satellites matches the expected value.
